# Build artifacts
bin/
# Root-level built binary only. Anchored with a leading slash so the
# pattern does NOT match the cmd/identuum-idp/ source directory.
/identuum-idp

# tools/api-docgen default staging output (the docs Hugo repo is the
# canonical home for generated YAML; the local staging dir is opt-in
# and should not be committed).
output/

# gograph local-only output
.gograph/

# Local development environment files — NEVER commit these.
# Copy dev.env.example to dev.env.local (or dev.env) and adjust for your setup.
dev.env
dev.env.local
dev.env.*.local
.env
.env.local
.env.*

# OS / editor artifacts
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
.idea/
.vscode/

# Go test artifacts
*.test
*.out
*.prof
coverage.out
coverage.html

# Go workspace files — never used in this repo ("No go.work at any
# level" is an enforced rule; see README Module hygiene). Ignored
# defensively so a locally-created workspace file (e.g. for ad-hoc
# multi-module linking while debugging a sibling repo) can never be
# accidentally committed.
go.work
go.work.sum

# Delve / VS Code Go debugger temp binaries. Can land in any package
# directory during a debug session, not just under .vscode/.
__debug_bin*

# Local/generated security artifacts
*.pem
*.key
*.lic
pinned_pg_cert.pem

# internal/tlscert.GenerateSelfSignedCert (exercised by
# generation_test.go) writes a self-signed cert + key into this
# directory, relative to the package under test.
tls_certs/

# Local-only coding-agent session guidance. AGENTS.md is intentionally
# NOT published — it is per-developer guidance that lives on disk and
# is excluded from the public repository.
AGENTS.md

# Local-only AI agent memory-consolidation outputs. These are
# per-developer reflective notes generated by Identuum memory-mcp
# tooling and are NEVER part of the public OSS surface.
docs/audit/
docs/design/


# Local-only MCP / AI tooling configuration (e.g. gograph MCP server
# binding). Per-developer; may carry tokens or local paths in future
# contributor checkouts. Never publish.
.mcp.json
.claude

# Root-level stray builds of ./tools/* — `go build ./tools/<name>` with no -o
# drops the binary at the repo root, and one such stray (`notrun`, a 3.8 MB
# Mach-O) was committed by a broad `git add` in a6840be and shipped inside the
# v0.3.0 source tag before THE-STRAY-BINARY removed it. One pattern per tool,
# not a glob: a glob wide enough to catch future tools would also swallow
# legitimately named files, and a new tool's entry is one line here plus the
# tracked-binary-check gate, which refuses the class outright either way.
/api-docgen
/clockfuse
/devseed
/notrun

# CI witness record (THE-UNWITNESSED-MIRROR): written by make ci-verify and
# uploaded as a CI artifact; never committed — a local run must not read as
# an edit to the committed GATE-RUN.txt record's tree digest.
/GATE-RUN.ci.txt
# The CI Integration Tests job's partial, commit-tied record; distinct from
# the local verify-integration record below.
/GATE-RUN.ci-integration.txt
# MINT-STATE.json is RETIRED (THE-ONE-MINT-RECORD, 2026-09-12): the mint's
# record of record is ../identuum-ui/GATE-RUN.e2e-full.txt, which the
# classifier now reads directly; nothing writes this marker any more. The
# ignore stays so a stale copy in an older checkout never enters the tree.
/MINT-STATE.json
# The integration profile's witness record (THE-UNRUN-SUITE, P-041):
# gitignored for the SAME reason as the CI record — a local run must not read
# as an edit to the committed GATE-RUN.txt record's tree digest, and two
# committed records would each stale the other. Re-check it on demand with
# `bash scripts/gate-witness.sh check . GATE-RUN.integration.txt`.
/GATE-RUN.integration.txt
TEST-spec.MD

# THE-CONFORMANCE-HARNESS: the suite clone lives OUTSIDE this repo
# (../.conformance-suite-cache, pinned by conformance/PIN) so the shared
# image-base gate never scans third-party Dockerfiles. Only the per-run
# TLS work dirs appear inside the tree:
# THE-CONFORMANCE-HARNESS: per-run TLS work dirs (teardown removes them)
/.conformance-work.*/

# THE-HONEST-HARNESS: a RED run keeps the suite's exported module logs
# (conformance/.evidence/<UTC stamp>/export) so a failure can be read after
# the teardown. A green run keeps nothing.
/conformance/.evidence/

# Legattus LEGACY files (THE-THREE-SMALL-ONES-OSS, 2026-09-19). These two
# entries guard files Legattus <= v0.1.3 wrote into a checkout: .legattus.json
# (per-checkout provider configuration) and .legattus/ (per-run lifecycle
# state and evidence). Since v0.1.4 (a59b24d) Legattus writes NEITHER — its
# state lives under $HOME/.local/state/legattus — and the ONE in-tree Legattus
# file is the committed .legattus-policy.json. The entries stay so a checkout
# that still carries the legacy files cannot dirty the tree: untracked-
# unignored paths make gate-witness `run` refuse to mint (THE-LAST-PASSWORD-
# DISARM, 2026-09-10, which added them when `legattus init` still created
# both). Nothing here is re-created by the current tool.
/.legattus.json
/.legattus/
